(FMT-42 — a branch-declared variable is usable FROM INSIDE FUNCTIONS,
 "exactly like a top-level declaration". It is — including the ordering
 defect a top-level declaration has: a function defined BEFORE the
 declaration reads a raw pointer instead of the text (see Discrepancy 3
 and D3.vox). Defined after, as here, it is correct. The claim as written
 holds; the probe is placed after the branch deliberately.
